<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhengzhou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhengzhou is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> province in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, a major railway hub near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>. Beneath the modern city lie the rammed-earth walls of an early Shang city of the Erligang period, about seven kilometres around, dating from about 1600 to 1400 BCE. It is one of the oldest walled cities known in China.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhengzhou.jpg" alt="Zhengzhou" width="320" height="188" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 白诗棋 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhengzhou_CBDcity.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
